Previous fix only changed the base .paper-chip rule but two rules in responsive.css were overriding it back to display:inline-flex:
  - .paper-chip-list .paper-chip { display: inline-flex; ... }
  - .paper-accordion-panel div.paper-chip, ... { display: inline-flex; ... }

Changed both to display:block so keyword spans inside chips flow as natural inline text without flex gaps breaking the sentence.

responsive.css bumped to v=2 for cache busting.

