Footer partial was executing SQL, violating MVC by mixing data access into a view. This change relocates sidebar contact retrieval into model/controller flow while keeping the footer view purely presentational.

- **Model-level data access**
  - Added `UserModel::getSidebarContacts` to encapsulate the friendships query.
- **Controller wiring**
  - Feed, saved, profile, and settings actions now pass `$sidebarContacts` to the view.
- **View cleanup**
  - Footer partial no longer touches the database; it uses the provided array.

```php
// Before (view)
$db = Database::getInstance()->getConnection();
$stmt = $db->prepare("SELECT ...");
$stmt->execute([$_SESSION['user_id']]);

// After (controller -> view)
$sidebarContacts = $this->userModel->getSidebarContacts($currentUserId);
```

Swaps the AI backend from Anthropic Claude to Google Gemini (`gemini-1.5-flash`) and updates the dependency accordingly.

## Changes

- **`routes/chat.js`**: Replace `@anthropic-ai/sdk` with `@google/generative-ai`. Use `GoogleGenerativeAI` client with `systemInstruction` support; map chat history roles (`assistant` → `model`) for Gemini's format; return `tokens_used: 0` (Gemini flash doesn't expose token counts in streaming responses).
- **`package.json`**: Remove `@anthropic-ai/sdk ^0.39.0`, add `@google/generative-ai ^0.21.0`.

```js
const genAI = new GoogleGenerativeAI(process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY);
const model = genAI.getGenerativeModel({ model: 'gemini-1.5-flash', systemInstruction: systemPrompt });
const chat = model.startChat({ history: chatHistory });
const result = await chat.sendMessage(message);
```

This PR adds an annotation to `test-utils` called `@WithStructDefs` that allows test writers to annotate classes with an ordered list of StructDef dependency classes to be registered before all other metadata objects.

## Usage

In the code below you will find an example for registering StructDefs defined by the "Car" class and the "Person" class using this new annotation. In this example, `Car` will be registered before `Person` based on their order.

```java
@LHTest
@WithStructDefs({Car.class, Person.class})
public class MyTestClass {
  // ...
}
```

`main.ts` had the core Slack fetch loop commented out, leaving the tool a no-op. This activates it and adds integration tests using the [`emulate`](https://github.com/vercel-labs/emulate) Slack emulator.

## Changes

- **`src/main.ts`** – Uncommented the `for await (const c of channelsIt())` loop that iterates channels, writes JSONL, and tracks progress dots
- **`src/settings.ts` / `src/lib/slack/slack.ts`** – Added `SLACK_BASE_URL` env var support; passed through as `baseUrl` to `SlackAPIClient` so the client can be redirected without code changes
- **`deno.json`** – Added `npm:emulate@^0.4.1`, `jsr:@std/assert`, and a `test` task (`deno test --allow-all --unstable-temporal src/`)
- **`src/main.test.ts`** – Two integration tests: JSONL output and Markdown export, both verified against real emulator state

## Test approach

The emulator is started at module top-level *before* `main.ts` is dynamically imported, ensuring the `SlackAPIClient` singleton in `slack.ts` picks up `SLACK_BASE_URL` on first evaluation:

```ts
const slackEmulator = await createEmulator({ service: "slack", port: 4003 });
Deno.env.set("SLACK_BASE_URL", slackEmulator.url);
Deno.env.set("INPUT_SLACKTOKEN", "test_token_admin");
// dynamic import so modules read the env vars above
const { default: main } = await import("./main.ts");
```

The emulator's default seed provides `#general` (`C000000001`) and `#random` (`C000000002`); tests post messages via `chat.postMessage` then assert on JSONL and `.md` output.

Astro's `ClientRouter` replaces `<html>` attributes on every page swap, stripping the `dark` class added by the theme toggle. The `is:inline` theme script in `BaseLayout.astro` only executes on initial page load, so the class was never restored on subsequent navigations.

## Changes

- **`src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro`** — Extract theme logic into `applyTheme()` and register it on `astro:after-swap`, so the correct theme is re-applied from `localStorage` after every View Transition swap:

```js
(function () {
  function applyTheme() {
    const theme = localStorage.getItem('theme');
    const systemDark = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches;
    if (theme === 'dark' || (!theme && systemDark)) {
      document.documentElement.classList.add('dark');
    } else {
      document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark');
    }
  }

  applyTheme();
  document.addEventListener('astro:after-swap', applyTheme);
})();
```

